<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valentinois</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Valentinois is a historic district of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valence">Valence</a>, on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>. Its counts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> family ruled it from the 12th century until 1419, when it passed to the Dauphiné and so to the French crown. It later became a ducal title, given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diane-de-poitiers">Diane de Poitiers</a>, and is still borne by the princes of Monaco.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentinois.jpg" alt="Valentinois" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Valentinois26 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valence_depuis_Crussol_(02)-002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
